{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2668239","formula":"SrAl₃(SO₄)(PO₄)(OH)₆","hill":"Al3H6O14PSSr","elements":["H","O","Al","P","S","Sr"],"composition":{"H":6.0,"O":14.0,"P":1.0,"S":1.0,"Al":3.0,"Sr":1.0},"names":{"en":"Svanbergite","ru":"Сванбергит","uk":"Сванбергіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Svanbergite is a colorless, yellow or reddish mineral with the chemical formula SrAl3(PO4)(SO4)(OH)6. It has rhombohedral crystals. It was first described for an occurrence in Varmland, Sweden in 1854 and named for Swedish chemist Lars Fredrik Svanberg (1805–1878).","ru":"Сванбергит — минерал SrAl3(PO4)(SO4)(OH)6, обычно либо бесцветен, либо окрашен в желтый, красновато-коричневый переходящий в розовый цвета. Открыт в 1854 году в Вермланде и назван в честь шведского химика Ларса Сванберга (1805-1878). Кристаллы сванбергита ромбоэдрической формы.","uk":"Сванбергіт (рос. сванбергит; англ. svanbergite; нім."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2668239","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Svanbergite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B1%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B3%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B1%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B3%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Svanbergite-Uvite-ea8c.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q2271409","formula":"CaAl₃(SO₄)(PO₄)(OH)₆","names":{"en":"Woodhouseite","ru":"Вудхаузеит"},"ele